WEBVTT

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.960
There you are, Your Highness.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:15.220
What might be the matter, Woshisu?

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:20.720
Your Highness, a message has arrived from the forces in Tusukuru.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.120
Three armies are insufficient?

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.980
Perhaps I underestimated Tusukuru.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:34.500
I would ask you for a little more time, Your Highness.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.490
General Raikou and the others will undoubtedly bring us victory.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.490
How kind you are.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.000
Surely you jest.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.820
Woshisu, I shall wait a little longer for your sake.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.500
Thank you, Your Highness.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.130
However...

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:56.060
We must consider our next move, should it become necessary.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.150
It seems I really cannot use it...

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:49.610
Do not engage the cavalry on their terms.

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:52.420
Hold formation and strike at them in groups!

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.600
We must break their formation.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:56.750
Follow me.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.390
Looks like it's true that they can't use them masks of theirs none.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:12.440
Not to mention they're up against a scary opponent.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:17.690
He's a class of his own, 
both as a warrior and a commander.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.960
<i>This is an important stop on the route to Onkamiyamukai.</i>

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:25.700
<i>Of course Tusukuru would bring its greatest power to defend it.</i>

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:29.450
<i>I expected him to be here.</i>

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:30.810
Let's go.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:41.340
Have you any ideas for how to deal with Tusukuru's fortress, Master Haku?

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:44.340
Well, I mean, I need to think...

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.440
We do not have the luxury of time.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:51.850
Why?

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:57.860
If <i>he</i> ever learns that we are struggling, he will act soon.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.360
Vurai?

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.320
Tusukuru is strong.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:07.680
Their soldiers and generals are beyond anything we've faced before.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:12.370
They've investigated the masks and know how to deal with them.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:18.380
But in the face of the man who was granted the 
ultimate power by the Emperor, that means nothing.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:21.950
Only soldiers should die on the battlefield.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.190
I never want to see that again.

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:33.060
Let's end this war, and fast.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.250
We got real close.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:40.380
Pretty amazin' that you knew about this path, Kuon-han.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.570
Nice work.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.790
This place is my home.

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:45.820
So what do we do now?

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:47.480
You know...

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.580
Even the strongest soldier can't fight on an empty stomach, right?

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:53.900
You sayin'...

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.970
We target their provisions.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:05:00.260
We sneak in while Munechika has the attention of their main force.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.460
How do we sneak in?

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:03.960
Well...

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:05.710
I'm counting on you two.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:06.930
Huh!?

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:11.110
You know, just make a path to take me to Old Man Mito.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.250
Like you always do.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:13.970
'Kay?

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:18.180
Can you not do it when everyone's watching?

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.830
Then you can stand a bit farther away...

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:25.340
Wait, can you only use that path yourselves or something?

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.490
That's a problem...

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:28.740
No.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:33.550
A caster in that fortress has erected a barrier.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.750
We cannot interfere from the outside.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.780
Counter-magic is a fundamental part of defense.

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:44.130
Their general is too competent to forget that.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.320
Really?

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.460
Yeah.

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:49.230
Then what?

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:50.360
What will you do?

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:51.690
What you gonna do?

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:53.290
Whatcha gonna do?

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.660
So that's it?

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:22.170
All right!

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:23.920
We'll break down the wall!

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.670
Yeah, not happening.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:28.420
Then we'll dig a hole to the inside!

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:30.430
With just the four o' us?

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:32.180
Then we flood the place!

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.930
Where will we get the water?

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:40.250
Reckon we should just go back for the time bein'.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.440
That's right.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.040
Come on, Haku.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:47.920
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:49.070
Let's go home for now.

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.890
Haku?

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:54.450
Why are you shifting your gaze?

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.040
I'm not.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:57.840
You are, aren't you?

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.580
I said I'm not.

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.620
You came up with an idea, didn't you?

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.060
I-I don't have any ideas...

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:08.600
Really?

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:09.640
Really.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:11.500
I see, I see!

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:14.970
You're not fooling anyone with that nonsense!

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:18.530
I feel like this hasn't happened in a while!

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:19.470
Spill the beans!

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:21.720
I haven't thought of anything!

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:25.070
Mister 'ere ain't usually this hardheaded.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:27.480
I wonder what kind of idea he's got.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:30.100
I'm going to squeeze it out of you no matter what!

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.990
My lips are sealed!

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:40.620
You're still not talking after all that?

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:43.370
I'll take it with me to the grave.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:48.880
Weren't you the one who said you wanted to end this war quickly?

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:54.510
Fine, damn it!

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.770
Listen up, Tusukuru forces!

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:03.930
Open your gates immediately!

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:09.250
We have a hostage!

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:13.280
She's a citizen of Tusukuru, 
and I can't guarantee her safety!

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:16.510
I'm the one who made him talk,

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.160
but I can't believe he came up with <i>this</i>.

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:20.830
You're a real scumbag, y'know.

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:23.290
See, this is why I didn't want to say it.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:29.120
Bit late to say this now, but there's one problem with this method.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:30.470
Which is?

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:36.450
It won't work if they don't believe Kuon's from Tusukuru.

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:39.160
You should have said that sooner!

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:42.460
If this falls through, we'll end up lookin' like pincushions!

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.810
That shouldn't be a problem.

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:58.070
Man, if looks could kill...

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:02.580
Some o' them are cryin'.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:07.330
Forget that. Hurry.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:09.330
That's right.

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:12.590
All right, now take us to the provisions storehouse!

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:16.440
That is, if you want this missy here back in one piece.

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:20.090
This way.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:24.220
This is it.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.150
Thanks, kid.

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:30.320
They're rollin' in food!

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.540
Are they eating better than we do in Yamato?

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:34.110
Just hurry up.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:38.600
It's a waste, but I guess I don't have a choice.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:39.670
Mister, heads up!

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:40.490
My lord, careful!

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:48.840
So very close...

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:51.330
<i>I knew he'd be here...</i>

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:56.480
My general said you were probably going to try something soon.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.400
On the ball, he was.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:03.640
Trying to set our food alight, were we?

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:07.350
I hope you didn't plan on leaving with your heads still attached.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:17.780
He's a tough bugger!

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:19.780
Not bad.

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:22.450
What's the problem? That all you got?

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:25.370
Entertain me a little more!

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:31.460
Whoa there!

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:36.960
Atui! Yakutowaruto!

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:40.220
Worrying about others? Aren't you a brave one.

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:41.580
Crap!

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:43.720
Wait! He's...

00:10:49.050 --> 00:10:50.600
<i>He didn't hold back.</i>

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.650
Whether you're a friend,

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:02.780
a parent, or a child...

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:06.280
If you're my enemy, I'll kill you!

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:16.290
Even you, the beloved child of the man I swore my soul to...

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:19.800
That is the law of the battlefield.

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:21.800
Kurou...

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:27.060
That's what it means to be on their side!

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:39.030
Am I wrong, young lady?

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:51.810
How are our losses?

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.270
Over ten percent.

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:58.340
Everyone is holding up well against the Rakusharai.

00:11:58.710 --> 00:12:01.120
We must buy a little more time...

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:06.340
For Haku and the others who went deep behind enemy lines.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:11.600
No matter how strong the enemy, 
or how fierce the battle, we will not withdraw.

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:16.350
As soldiers of Munechika, that is who we are.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.460
Indeed.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:26.360
All troops, stand ready.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:28.080
We shall repel the enemy!

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:38.910
That's strange.

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:41.880
I expected more from you, young lady.

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:46.890
See? Just like that...

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:50.890
Have you been slacking on your training since you left?

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:54.890
You shouldn't assume I love war the way you do.

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:01.570
Do you really intend to kill me?

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:03.880
You're begging for your life now?

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:05.360
I'm just asking.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:09.660
Can you forgive me for betraying my country... 
For betraying all of you?

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:11.220
Betraying?

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:14.160
Don't be stupid.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:19.470
A little shrimp like you mixing in with the soldiers and fighting us

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:23.170
does no more harm than a bug's sting, from our perspective.

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:26.410
I'm right, aren't I?

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:31.730
If you were serious, you could tear this country in half.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:37.560
If you're not doing that, 
it means you're just here to play.

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:41.660
Do you know how much I 
agonized over coming here?

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:43.320
And you say I'm playing?

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:45.420
Am I wrong?

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:46.900
Then...

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:49.950
K-Kurou?

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:51.570
What?

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:54.490
I-Is Sister Aruruu doing well?

00:13:54.490 --> 00:13:56.330
Sure, I guess.

00:13:56.710 --> 00:14:00.180
Does she still go on hunts for honey?

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:01.900
She does, but...

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:08.420
R-Right, right!

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:10.610
Speaking of Sister Aruruu...

00:14:10.610 --> 00:14:12.850
Is Sister Kamyu doing well, too?

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:19.600
Where do you think <i>you're</i> going?

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:21.600
He caught me!

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:24.610
You got guts, kid.

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:27.860
I was so close...

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:30.110
I guess I don't have a choice anymore.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:32.120
I'll set fire to it now!

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:33.620
The hell you will!

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:43.630
So you were holding back before, huh?

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:49.880
Who was it that taught me to hold her trump card until the very end?{DO THEY EVEN HAVE CARDS IN THIS UNIVERSE???}

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:53.010
I'm glad you remembered.

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:55.890
In that case...

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.790
So close.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:03.640
He dodged that <i>too</i>?

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:05.520
Talk about killing my confidence.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:11.030
Young lady, you...

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:17.450
If he's here, then I knew you would be too, Kurou.

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:20.900
It would be too dangerous to fight you head-on.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:24.830
So I used trickery.

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:28.300
I'm ending this war, one way or another!

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:29.800
I see.

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:32.800
Interesting!

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:36.400
Okay, you two, now we get serious.

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:38.370
You can defeat him now!

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:41.300
Um, Kuon-han?

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:42.300
What?

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:45.110
I've been serious this whole time, y'know.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:48.560
Same here. I was giving all I had.

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:50.070
Um...

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:55.820
You're not getting out of here alive.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:10.710
Master Haku, is it time yet?

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:13.720
This seems like a good spot...

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:14.620
Okay.

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:19.770
Kuon?

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:21.140
You okay?

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:24.850
Yeah, but he is really strong.

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:29.360
Hey there, kid.

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:31.360
You ready?

00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:33.860
Ready for what?

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.090
What else?

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:38.660
Ready to meet your maker!

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.400
You just don't know when to give up!

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:52.260
You got that right!

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:55.370
Stop screwing around!

00:16:56.930 --> 00:17:01.260
<i>I'm not gonna die here.</i>

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:02.770
You ain't going anywhere!

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.470
Checkmate.

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:15.030
Now die!

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:23.290
You... That's...

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:28.540
Kuon, get out of here!

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.050
I won't let you escape!

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:00.820
That was...

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:02.830
He did it!

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:04.830
All forces, retreat.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:06.360
Make haste to the fortress!

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:12.100
Strike them down!

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:14.090
All forces, follow me!

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:24.850
I'll kindly ask you to stay for a while longer

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:28.600
until our ally who attacked your fortress escapes.

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:38.610
He must be quite a man if he's worth all this.

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:44.240
He gives me the feeling that he's about to accomplish something.

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:46.290
I see.

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:49.040
I'll only say this once.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:51.370
Stand aside.

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:54.880
Not while I still draw breath.

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:57.400
How regrettable...

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:04.890
I am Tusukuru's Samurai General, Benawi.

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:09.390
I am one of Yamato's Eight Pillar Generals, Munechika.

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:10.390
En garde!

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:23.740
<i>I can't believe my memories of back then came in handy.</i>

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:26.460
Okay, let's get out of here!

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:27.990
Yeah.

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:29.750
Man, that <i>really</i> hurt...

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:32.510
I thought I was a goner.

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:35.300
He survived that!?

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:37.000
Is he a monster?

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:41.270
Let's pick up where we left off, shall we?

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:44.760
Master...

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:47.260
We have come for you.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.010
I'm saved!

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:51.020
Oh, no you don't!

00:19:59.100 --> 00:19:59.910
Hey!

00:20:01.060 --> 00:20:02.280
What?

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:07.150
Was it your idea to use the young lady as a hostage?

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:08.730
That's right.

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.290
What's your name, young man?{THE SEASON ONE MUSIC}

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:15.040
It's Haku.

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:24.550
Haku...

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:26.910
That name... That fan...

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:29.680
I see.

00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:32.920
So that's him, young lady?

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:46.040
Even your strength exceeds mine.

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:48.950
But I will not be killed easily!

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:53.980
This sound...

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:55.410
It's the signal to withdraw!

00:20:57.310 --> 00:21:00.010
I know... But...

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.470
This battle will be concluded another day.

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:10.180
Indeed it will.

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:12.470
All forces, retreat!

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:14.480
We're returning to base.

00:22:58.180 --> 00:23:02.030
What do you mean Raikou and the others withdrew?

00:23:03.490 --> 00:23:05.320
Hey, Munechika?

00:23:08.690 --> 00:23:12.720
We've received an urgent message from Yamato.

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:17.840
What happened?

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:20.980
The Emperor...

00:23:21.950 --> 00:23:23.580
is dead.

00:23:27.110 --> 00:23:29.940
